==English==
[[File:Chinese colporteur selling scriptures.png|thumb|Chinese [[colporter]] selling scriptures in Peking (1902)]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|scrīptūra||a writing, scripture}}, from {{m|la|scrīptum}}, the supine of {{m|la|scrībō||I write}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈskɹɪptʃɚ/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈskɹɪptʃə/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-scripture.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyph|en|scrip|ture}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[sacred]] [[writing]] or [[holy]] [[book]].
#: ''The primary '''scripture''' in Zoroastrianism is the Avesta.''
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Leander Keck|title=Who is Jesus?|isbn=0567088332|page=143|passage=It would be quite unwise to deem the whole historical enterprise as wrong-headed and to think that one can revert to the gospels' way of reading '''scripture''', {{...}}}}# {{lb|en|by extension}} An [[authoritative]] [[statement]].

